cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Velri-lib: C23 Tensor, Execution Graph, and Khronos Slang AOT Compute Library"
message: "If you use Velri-lib in software, benchmarks, or research, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "Vemloir"
version: "0.7.0"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
license: GPL-3.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/velri-inference/velri-lib"
url: "https://velri-inference.github.io"
abstract: >-
  Velri-lib is a standalone C23 neural-network computation library providing zero-copy
  tensor views, liveness scratch memory planning, UMA-aware execution graphs, reusable
  transformer blocks, and modular Khronos Slang ahead-of-time (AOT) kernels for CPU
  (AVX2, AVX-512 VNNI, ARM64, RISC-V 64) and Vulkan 1.3 / SPIR-V 1.6.
keywords:
  - c23
  - khronos-slang
  - aot-compilation
  - vulkan-compute
  - spir-v
  - cooperative-matrix
  - gemm
  - blis
  - flash-attention
  - avx512
  - neural-network-library
  - llm-inference
